From 37f5cfd1a4644c51595ac8086bd01dd936330534 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:39:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban chat links: a card on a profile's own board
 stays its chat's under links_reader=replica

Five whys (t_01a1d49646d816af, laptop-1 links_diff, 2026-11-13):
1. links_diff('macbook') stayed unclean on one row after PR #2163: chat
   20261028_160313_544eef -> hub card t_d3e3f88a (bb-tuner, ready).
2. The replica has no task row and no link row for it; the Board refused
   MBP's link push (gateway.error.log 2026-10-28 17:22:31: rejected
   not_found: no task t_d3e3f88a).
3. The card lives in the hub's profiles/bb-tuner/kanban.db, not the shared
   root board: hermes-hub's qualified owner route (`-p <profile> kanban`)
   points HERMES_KANBAN_HOME at the owner profile's own home, and its
   collector publishes those boards under qualified keys
   (<gw>/<profile>/<board>/<id>), so the origin ledger has the card.
4. Board sync carries only a gateway's shared kanban home
   (kanban_sync_client.board_paths / kanban_db.kanban_home: shared across
   profiles by design), so a profile-own board never reaches the Board.
5. replica_cards answered only from replica links, so with
   links_reader=replica such a card vanished from its chat's task list and
   sidebar count, while the ledger reader showed it.

Shape (read-only, 2026-11-13): only the hub has profile-own boards
(profiles/bb-tuner/kanban.db: 1 card, t_d3e3f88a, open; profiles/ci-sweeper/
kanban.db: 1 archived probe card). laptop-1, the mini and worker-5 have none.

Fix: syncing those boards would contradict core's one-shared-board design,
so the reader keeps them from the ledger instead:
- `_is_profile_board_card`: a qualified ledger row whose owner profile is
  not `default`.
- `replica_cards` adds this gateway's chats' unreleased profile-board
  obligations from the ledger (source `ledger-profile-board`) unless a
  readable replica carries a task row for that id, in which case the
  replica's links and release still decide. One ledger read per call
  (`_ledger_index`, memoised with the owner labels) serves both.
- `links_diff` counts them in `profile_board_links` (also printed by
  `hermes kanban sync links-diff`): the reader's own answer, not a
  difference. Real default-profile gaps stay visible.

Tests: two new tests in test_kanban_chat_links.py (reader keeps the card,
session_tasks/active_task_counts list it, links_diff clean with
profile_board_links=1; a replica that carries the card keeps its own
answer, an unsynced board answers from the ledger). Both fail on the base.
Updated test_kanban_run_machine to stub `_ledger_index`, and the stale_ok
fallback test to check every ledger read keeps the policy (the cold
fallback and the profile-board read are now two reads).
